## PR Title
Overhaul Tests + Errors for Checkbox (deprecated) and CheckboxV1

## PR Description
### Platforms Impacted
- [ ] iOS
- [ ] macOS
- [x] win32 (Office)
- [x] windows
- [ ] android

### Description of changes

Previously a part of #2423, split to be more managable.

Currently, for most developers, it is difficult to figure out what the root issue is when a FURN E2E test fails because of opaque error messages. The existing E2E tests are also in need of some clean up in terms of code and PageObject design. 

This PR is part of a larger effort to address the above. Here, I've updated error messages, use new BasePage methods, and did general cleanup for the following tests:
- Checkbox (deprecated)
- CheckboxV1

This PR also re-enables previously disabled functional tests for the deprecated Checkbox on windows.

#### Removal of Selectors

One big change to the tests across the board is the removal of Selector enums within tests. Previously, Selectors were used to choose which element was to be clicked, get an attribute from, etc. However, because many tests required different selectors from the base `ComponentSelector` in BasePage.ts to select test elements, this meant that different Page Objects ended up implementing the same methods (`sendKey()`, `click()`, and other attribute testing methods). 

In removing selectors, we can re-use methods for doing most things a test requires implemented in BasePage.ts and pass WebdriverIO elements directly (see [`compareAttribute()`](https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-react-native/blob/3500d25b492a0fba0df3ab478b09d2775b78e452/apps/E2E/src/common/BasePage.ts#L80-L93),[ `click()`](https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-react-native/blob/3500d25b492a0fba0df3ab478b09d2775b78e452/apps/E2E/src/common/BasePage.ts#L127-L130), and [`sendKeys()`](https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-react-native/blob/3500d25b492a0fba0df3ab478b09d2775b78e452/apps/E2E/src/common/BasePage.ts#L132-L134)). This way, future Page Objects remain light and only implement getters or other methods needed for the specific test.

This doesn't mean that Selectors can't be used. Taking the [FocusZone test](https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-react-native/blob/3500d25b492a0fba0df3ab478b09d2775b78e452/apps/E2E/src/FocusZone/pages/FocusZonePageObject.ts#L18-L28), the large amount of elements used within the test let us use a Selector Enum to pick out specific elements to pass in. But for most cases, we can rely on a small amount of getters and the reusable BasePage methods for creating a test.

### Verification

Tests pass in the CI and locally. 

### Pull request checklist

This PR has considered (when applicable):
- [x] Automated Tests
- [ ] Documentation and examples
- [ ] Keyboard Accessibility
- [ ] Voiceover
- [ ] Internationalization and Right-to-left Layouts


