## PR Title
Immutable parser model

## PR Description
### Description 

This PR makes the Parser's model immutable.

Reviewers notes:
- the PR focuses around making the model immutable.  For each:
    - I've fixed any issues where constructors or static methods don't throw NPEs on null args.
    - I've fixed any issues with `hashCode` and `equals` impls.
    - I've standardised on two constructors, (one with no `location` the other with an optional `location`).
    - where issues were found I've generally added a test to match. Some model's still have no tests.
- All the model changes should be non-controversial, and have tests added, so don't need thorough reviewing. (Thankfully, given there are a lot!).
- Previously, there was complexity in model constructors around the `NodeLocation`. Some constructors too one, others didn't and there was generally a `private` on that took an `Optional<NodeLocation`.  This led to overly complex code, especially in `StatementRewritter`. So, as mentioned above, I've switched all models to have two constructors, one with no location and one with an optional location. The former should _generally_ only be used from tests, (and we might want to remove it totally), the latter is used from production code.
- The above massively simplifies `StatementRewritter`.
- I've added `ParserModelTest` which will go through each class derived from `Node` and ensure:
   - It's annotated with `@Immutable`, (the _errorprone_ one as it is available at runtime).
   - all fields are `final`.
   - all fields are of immutable types, (including looking deep into collections and maps).
   - all constructors through NPEs on null params
   - all public static methods through NPEs on null params.
- WIth an immutable model I've obviously had to fix up a few locations in the code - most notable `FunctionCall` was previously mutated by `AggregateAnalyzer`, which added a `defaultParameter` if the function has no params.   This involved changes to `AggregateAnalyzer` and `ExpressionTypeManager.visitFunctionCall`, which are worth looking at in more detail.

### Testing done 
Lots of tests added, very little functionality actually changes.

### Reviewer checklist
- [ ] Ensure docs are updated if necessary. (eg. if a user visible feature is being added or changed).
- [ ] Ensure relevant issues are linked (description should include text like "Fixes #<issue number>")



