## PR Title
Minor refactoring and a bug fix in 'game-core'.

## PR Description
## Overview

Minor refactoring and a bug fix in 'game-core'. Apart from the bug fix, there should be no changes in behaviour.

## Testing Performed

Only light testing performed, including a quick session against the Hard AI (which I assume corresponds to the "Pro" AI in the source code).

EDIT: A unit test has been added.

## Additional Review Notes

~`verify` was run and completed successfully. However, I am in doubt about how to best test the changes. Would it make sense to look into creating a unit test for some of them, or would that be overkill?~

The first commit refactors a method in TriggerAttachment.java to make it more concise and maintainable, and fixes a bug in ProTerritory.java discovered through usage of linters (IntelliJ's built-in "Inspect Code..." as well as the SonarLint plugin for IntelliJ). The second commit is meant to refactor ProTerritory.java such that such bugs can more easily be avoided in the future.

