## PR Title
Feature/remove participant submission

## PR Description
<!-- Thanks for contributing to Artemis! Before you submit your pull request, please make sure to check the following boxes by putting an x in the [ ] (don't: [x ], [ x], do: [x]) -->
<!-- If your pull request is not ready for review yet, create a draft pull request! -->

### Checklist
- [X] I tested the changes and all related features on the test server https://artemistest.ase.in.tum.de.
- [x] I documented my source code using the JavaDoc / JSDoc style.
- [x] I added integration test cases for the server (Spring) related to the features
- [x] I added integration test cases for the client (Jest) related to the features
- [X] I added screenshots/screencast of my UI changes
- [X] I translated all the newly inserted strings

### Motivation and Context
In some cases, it is seen that a participant/student is able to submit multiple submissions for the same exercise, due to which a participant can be graded differently by different tutors with different grades. This led to an inconsistent score of the participant and the instructors had to manually remove the submission in the database to solve this issue.

This feature aims to reduce the complicated tasks the instructors have to go through in order to remove a duplicated submission. 

### Description
When a participationId is clicked on the list of participations of an exercise, it opens a page that lists all the submissions submitted under that particular participationId. The list displays the submissionId, submissionType (manual or automatic), submissionDate, result and assessor so that it is easier for the instructor to identify which one has to be removed. When clicked on the "Delete" button, it displays a confirmation dialog, which when clicked deletes that particular submission from the database.

### Steps for Testing

1. Log in to Artemis
2. Navigate to Course Administration
3. Click on the "Exercises" button of a course under which the exercise was created
4. Click on the "Participations" button of the particular exercise. This opens a page that lists all the participants of that exercise.
5. Click on the "ParticipationID" of the participation whose submission has to be modified. This opens a page that lists all the submissions submitted under that particular participantId.
6. According to the description provided in the list, it is easier for the Instructor to decide which of the duplicated submissions (if exists) has to be deleted.
7. Click on the "Delete" button. This opens a popup for confirmation of the delete operation. Clicking "Delete" of the popup deletes the submission.

