## PR Title
Button Component

## PR Description
### Overview
Adds a `Button` component type, which leverages the existing `Image` and `Text` elements. Supports two different transition modes, `Tint` and `Sprite Change`:

<img width="347" alt="screen shot 2018-05-10 at 18 52 01" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/37333094/39884970-5f651f78-5483-11e8-91c5-37285a00dc7f.png">

<img width="346" alt="screen shot 2018-05-10 at 18 52 30" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/37333094/39884977-63448f52-5483-11e8-94a9-23e4d96fc209.png">

### Current Status
I've got a few of things left to do:
- [x] Implement tint animation/tweening.
- [x] Further testing on various combinations of component addition/removal, Image reference re-assignment, Image sprite modification, etc. There are couple of issues here that I'm aware of.
- [x] Implement `touchleave` support in `element-input.js`. On a machine with a mouse, the button will automatically revert to the default state if the user presses on it but then moves the mouse away from the button. On a phone this doesn't happen, which it appears is because we don't currently implement `touchleave`.

