## PR Title
ev/organise services

## PR Description
## Foundations 
[[ch2283]](https://app.clubhouse.io/mycrypto/story/2283/move-re-order-files-as-first-step-to-creating-an-orm-api-to-talk-to-local-storage)
The goal of this PR is to have a place for everything (_just about everything_), so we can easily know where to find services and utils, and easily understand the data flow throughout the app.

This PR untangles `libs`, `providers` and `services` by creating:
```
- services
   - ApiService        // Other HTTP calls
   - EthService        // Network connections and chain helpers
   - Store             // For React to interact with App Data
   - ...
```

- Shared data types have been moved to `v2/types`
- Shared data `constants` moved to `v2/config`
- Shared helpers not related to Ethereum are moved to `v2/utils`
- The three remaining `providers` that will be migrated in the future.

## Conventions
There are a few conventions adopted during this migration that I propose we stick to until we get can refactor the services.
- **explicit `exports` from folders**. This is to help us determine the api for each service and facilitate future refactors.
- **a react component never imports from a file**. When a react component imports a service or a method, we import from the `index.ts` of the folder e.g Store, ApiService, EthService. By decoupling components and services we facilitate changes within the service. 
- **`v2/utils` is restricted to pure functions** and preferably single file functions.
- I tried to delete all the code from `v2/libs` that wasn't used in `v2`. If you need anything, before coding it yourself, look under `common/libs` and copy the code to `EthService`!


## Continuous improvement
Now that we have a decent file organisation, we can gradually improve the codebase with each commit by introducing `Controller` components that respect the following flow:
```
Pure Component -> Controller -> Store 
                                                   |-> EthService
                                                   |-> ApiService
```
Ideally a Component will only interact with the `Provider` in `Store` who should present the data in the correct format for the component to consume and handle all interaction with the persistence layer.

------
NB: 
This PR touches a looot of files! I intentionally avoided any logic changes, though some may have slip by. 
- To facilitate the review I suggest you pull and test locally. 
- To facilitate the rebase I'll squash the commits into a single one once it's approved

